      "title": "Employment",
      "description": "­ Employment - Cornell College Skip Navigation. Students Faculty/Staff Parents/Families Alumni Give About Academics Admission Financial Aid Athletics Student Life Virtual Tour Menu Search Search Search About Students Academics Faculty & Staff Admission Parents & Families Financial Aid Alumni Athletics Give Virtual Tour Student Life Transfer Cornell on Facebook Cornell on Twitter Cornell on Instagram Cornell on Flickr Cornell on Youtube Search Search Search Directory search Campus calendar Academic calendar Dining Cole Library Bookstore Cornell on Facebook Cornell on Twitter Cornell on Instagram Cornell on Flickr Cornell on Youtube Employment Job openings Cornell is committed to attracting, selecting, retaining, and developing a quality workforce in a positive work environment. For a listing of positions that are currently available, please refer to the following pages: Faculty and staff positions Student Job Board Staff Hiring Process Curious as to what the application and hiring process at Cornell will look like? We've provided a basic outline of the employee hiring process to fill you in on what you can expect. What are the benefits? In addition to gaining a stylish purple wardrobe and a beautiful working environment on our campus, there are many benefits to working at Cornell. See a summary of staff and faculty benefits . Important notices for applicants Cornell College participates in E-Verify for employment eligibility verification Right to work notice Cornell College complies with Iowa's Smoke-Free Air Act and restricts smoking of tobacco products, electronic cigarettes, vaping, and similar smoking methods on campus Cornell's crime & safety policy and procedures View Cornell's campus crime statistics Resources Resources for job seekers To aid prospective employees in the application process, we have compiled an index to information on the college and the Mount Vernon area. About Cornell Resources for job seekers Resources for Cornell managers Request to contract services What are you waiting for? At Cornell College, faculty and staff members are not just colleagues and co-workers — we're family. Do you have what it takes to rock the purple and white? Join us! Apply now Request Info Visit Cornell Apply Now Cookie Policy Cornell College asks you to accept cookies for authorization purposes,\n\t\t\t\t    as well as to track usage data and for marketing purposes. To get more information about these cookies and the processing of your personal information, please see our Privacy Policy . Do you accept these cookies and the\n\t\t\t\t    processing of your personal information involved? Accept all cookies Necessary cookies only Cornell shield Support Cornell Cornell College 600 First Street SW Mount Vernon, IA 52314 319.895.4000 Contact Cornell Visitor Info Cole Library Campus Calendar News Jobs Emergencies Consumer Info & Accreditation Directory Privacy Policy Web Accessibility Web Feedback Site Map CTCL Logo Cornell College admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally accorded or made available to students. Cornell does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national and ethnic origin in administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, scholarship and loan programs, and athletic and other school-administered programs. © 2026  Cornell College. All rights reserved."
